          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong Courant algebroid
            – or better:
            %strong Courant Lie 2-algebroid
            – (named after
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Courant"} Theodore Courant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie 2-algebroid
            (
            %a{:href => "#RoytenbergStructure"}> Roytenberg
            ):
          %p
            it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroid"} Lie 2-algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{P}
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{P})
            is equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+n-algebra"} Poisson 3-algebra
            whose Poisson bracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo :
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{-,-\} : CE(\mathfrak{P})\otimes CE(\mathfrak{P})
                  \\to
                  CE(\mathfrak{P})
          %p of degree -2 is non-degenerate.
          %p
            Therefore the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{CE(\mathfrak{P})}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{P})
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            with respect to this bracket in that there is an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta \in CE(\mathfrak{P})
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{P})} = \{\Theta, -\}
                  \\,.
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The concept of Courant algebroids was originally introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Irene+Dorfman"} Irene Dorfman
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ted+Courant"} Ted Courant
            to study
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            in the presence of constraints. Later it was considered by Liu,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
            in the study of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+Lie+algebroids"} double Lie algebroids
          %p
            In these parts of the literature Courant algebroids are considered in the form of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
          %ul
            %li
              %p in one there is a skew-symmetric bracket which fails to satisfy a Jacobi identity by a coherent term – this is the Courant bracket definition proper;
            %li
              %p in the other there is a bracket which satisfies a Jacobi identity but is skew-symmetric only up to a correction term – this is the Dorfman version.
          %p
            So there are several different ways to present the structure encoded in a Courant algebroid. The picture that seems to be emerging is that the
            %em true
            meaning of the notoin of Courant algebroids is given by the notion of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} 2-symplectic manifold
          %p
            Moreover, the way
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Rinehart+algebra"} Lie-Rinehart algebra
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant-Dorfman+algebra"} Courant-Dorfman algebra
          %hr/
          %p (… need to say more about the way the Courant Lie algebroid is obtained from a Lie bialgebroid by derived brackets …)
          %hr/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#lie_algebras_of_compact_type Lie algebras of compact type
          %p
            A Courant Lie 2-algebroid over the point is precisely an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            that is equipped with a quadratic and non-degenerate
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
          %h3#standard_courant_algebroid_and_gerbes
            Standard Courant algebroid and
            = succeed "-gerbes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Courant+algebroid"} standard Courant algebroid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the one which
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                with extra structure is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo =
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊕
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = T X\oplus T^* X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                and the cotangent bundle; with
              %ul
                %li
                  %p bilinear form
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo +
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo =
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\langle X + \xi , Y +\eta \rangle = \eta(X) + \xi(Y)
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in \Gamma(T X)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi η
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi, \eta \in \Gamma(T^* X)
              %ul
                %li
                  %p brackets
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo +
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi ℒ
                            %mi X
                          %mi η
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mi ℒ
                            %mi Y
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo +
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          [X + \xi, Y + \eta] = [X,Y] + \mathcal{L}_X \eta
                          \- \mathcal{L}_Y \xi + \frac{1}{2} d (\eta(X) - \xi(Y))
                  %p
                    where
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℒ
                            %mi X
                          %mi η
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mi η
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_X \eta = \{d,\iota_X\} \eta
                    denotes the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+derivative"} Lie derivative
                    of the 1-form
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi η
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                    by the vector field
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*[2] T[1] X
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+tangent+bundle"} shifted tangent bundle
              %p
                where the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
                is on each local
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+patch"} coordinate patch
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \simeq U \subset X
                with coordinates
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^i\}
                in degree 0,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{d x^i\}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_i\}
                in degree 1 and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_i\}
                in degree 2 given by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mi C
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mi dR
                              %mo +
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi i
                              %mfrac
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi i
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msup
                                %mi dx
                                %mi i
                              %mfrac
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msup
                                    %mi x
                                    %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi i
                              %mfrac
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      d_C &amp;= d_{dR} + p_i \frac{\partial}{\partial \theta_i}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;= dx^i \frac{\partial}{\partial x^i }
                      + p_i \frac{\partial}{\partial \theta_i}
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,.
          %p
            Such a standard Courant algebroid may be understood as the higher analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
            of a line bundle. See below in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#RelationToAtiyahGroupoids"} Relation to Atiyah groupoids
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#generalized_complex_geometry Generalized complex geometry
          %p
            The study of Courant algebroids is to a large extent known as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
          %h3#chernsimons_element_and_courant_model
            Chern-Simons element and Courant
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            As every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            on a Courant Lie 2-algebroid transgresses to a cocycle in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid+cohomology"} ∞-Lie algebroid cohomology
            and this transgression is witnessed by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            induced by this element is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+sigma-model"} Courant sigma-model
          %h3#lagrangian_submanifolds_and_dirac_structures Lagrangian submanifolds and Dirac structures
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+dg-submanifolds"} Lagrangian dg-submanifolds
            of a Courant Lie 2-algebroid corespond to its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+structures"} Dirac structures
          %h3#RelationToAtiyahGroupoids Relation to Atiyah Lie 2-algebroid and quantomorphism 2-group
          %p We discuss how the following tower of notions works
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle"} circle n-bundle
                  with
                  = succeed "-form" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebra"} Lie n-algebra
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+bisections"} of bisections
                  of Atiyah Lie n-group
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle"} circle 2-bundle
                  with 1-form connection
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+2-algebroid"} Courant Lie 2-algebroid
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,k \in \mathbb{N}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leq n
            write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi DK
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi log
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %mn 0
                          %mo →
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo →
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^k}
                  \\coloneqq
                  DK\left[
                  U(1) \stackrel{d log}{\to}
                  \\Omega^1
                  \\stackrel{d}{\to}
                  \\cdots
                  \\stackrel{d}{\to}
                  \\Omega^{k-1}
                  \\stackrel{d}{\to} \Omega^k
                  \\to
                  \\underbrace{
                  0
                  \\to 0
                  \\to \cdots
                  \\to 0
                  }_{n-k}
                  \\right]
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            which is presented under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohomology+diagram#DeligneCoefficients"} differential cohomology diagram – Examples – Deligne coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
            we have the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^n} \simeq \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
            we have the moduli
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle n-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^0} \simeq \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 2
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_2 \lt k_1
            there are evident truncation maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^{k_1}}
                  \\to
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^{k_2}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla \;\colon\; X \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            modulates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"}> bundle (n-1)-gerbe
            ), which we may think of as a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"} prequantum circle n-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}
            this has an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concretification"} concretification
            of this (…) is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-group"} quantomorphism n-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QuantMorph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QuantMorph(\nabla)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi QuantMorph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi conc
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ∇
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ∇
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi n
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{QuantMorph}(\nabla)
                  \\coloneqq
                  conc\mathbf{Aut}(\nabla)
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp; \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to} &amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\nabla}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\nabla}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            But we can also first forget the
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ∇
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla_{n-1}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  X
                  \\stackrel{\nabla}{\to}
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^n}
                  \\to
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^{n-1}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            this is sometimes known in the literature as a “bundle gerbe with connective structure but without curving”.
          %p
            The concretified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of that truncated connection is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+bisections"} of bisection
            of the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Atiyah n-groupoid
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Atiyah+n-groupoid"} ?
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi conc
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  conc \mathbf{Aut}(\nabla_{n-1}) \in Grp(Smooth \infty Grpd)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+bisections"} group of bisections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie groupoid
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+principal+bundle"} circle principal bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_0 \colon X \to \mathbf{B} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of sections of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            of sections of the corresponding Courant Lie 2-algebroid. With a little bit of translation, this is what is shown in (
            %a{:href => "#Collier"}> Collier
            ).
          %p
            Finally notice that the forgetful map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn^{n-1}}
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi conc
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi conc
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  conc \mathbf{Aut}(\nabla) \to conc \mathbf{Aut}(\nabla_{n-1})
          %p
            hence an embedding of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-group"} quantomorphism n-group
            into the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+bisections"} group of bisections
            of the Atiyah n-groupoid. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            and after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+2-algebra"} Poisson Lie 2-algebra
            into the sections of the Courant Lie 2-algebroid. This embedding had been observed in (
            %a{:href => "#Rogers"}> Rogers
            ).
