                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.00265"} arXiv:1707.00265
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Courant algebroids and strongly homotopy Lie algebras
                = succeed "(1):81-93," do
                  %strong 46
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                ,
                %em Courant algebroids, derived brackets and even symplectic supermanifolds
                PhD
              %p
                thesis, University of California, Berkeley, 1999. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.DG/9910078"}> math.DG/9910078
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+%C5%A0evera"}> Pavol Ševera
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some title containing the words “homotopy” and “symplectic”, e.g. this one
              %p mathématiques. Fasc. XVI, chapter Trav. Math., XVI, pp. 121-137. Univ. Luxembourg, 2005.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the structure of graded symplectic supermanifolds and Courant algebroids
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 315
                %em Quantization, Poisson brackets and beyond
                (Manchester, 2001), Theodore Voronov, editor, Amer. Math. Soc. 2002.
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203110"}> arXiv:math/0203110
                )
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
              ,
              %em Quasi-Lie bialgebroids and twisted Poisson manifolds
              , Letters in Mathematical
              %p
                Physics, 61(2):123-137 (2002) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0112152"}> arXiv:math/0112152
                )
          %p Another useful summary of the theory of Courant algebroids is in of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Gualtieri"}> Marco Gualtieri
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0401/0401221v1.pdf#page=19"} section 3
              of:
              %em Generalized complex geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0401221"}> arXiv:math/0401221
              )
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            between Courant algebroids:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Vysoky"}> Jan Vysoky
              ,
              %em Hitchhiker’s Guide to Courant Algebroid Relations
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.05347"}> arXiv:1910.05347
              )
          %p
            A discussion of Courant algebroids with an eye towards the relation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Courant+algebroid"} standard Courant algebroid
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Bressler"}> Paul Bressler
              , Alexander Chervov,
              %em Courant algebroids
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0212195"}> hep-th/0212195
              )
          %p
            The identification of the Lie 2-algebra of sctions of a Courant Lie 2-algebroid associated with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            as its Lie algebra of automorphisms after forgetting the “curving” is in
          %ul#Collier
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Braxton+Collier"}> Braxton Collier
              ,
              %em Infinitesimal Symmetries of Dixmier-Douady Gerbes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.1525"}> arXiv:1108.1525
              )
          %p
            The embedding of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+2-algebra"} Poisson Lie 2-algebra
            of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            of sections of the Courant Lie 2-algebroid of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+2-bundle"} prequantum 2-bundle
            is observed in
          %ul#Rogers
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Courant algebroids from categorified symplectic geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.0040"} arXiv:1001.0040
          %p This is developed further in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+of+local+observables+from+higher+prequantum+bundles"} L-∞ algebras of local observables from higher prequantum bundles
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.6292"}> arXiv:1304.6292
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Courant_algebroid"} Courant algebroid
          %p
            The relation between the two different Lie-algebroid-like definition of Courant algebroids, one with skew, the other with non-skew brackets inspired on the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} Lie 2-algebras
            the treatment
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                ,
                %em On weak Lie 2-algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.3461"}> arXiv/0712.3461
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 2-plectic geometry, Courant algebroids, and categorified prequantization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.2975"} arxiv:1009.2975
          %p
            A proposal for a higher analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Courant+algebroid"} standard Courant algebroid
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus T^* X
            replaced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus \wedge^n T^* X
            – for a notion of standard
            %span.newWikiWord
              higher Courant Lie algebroid
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/higher+Courant+Lie+algebroid"} ?
            – is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Zambon"}> Marco Zambon
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  \-algebras and higher analogues of Dirac structures and Courant algebroids
              = succeed ":4" do
                %strong 10
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1003.1004"} arXiv:1003.1004
              %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an:1260.53134"} Zbl:1260.53134
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/JSG.2012.v10.n4.a4"} doi
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Chern-Weil+Derivation+of+AKSZ+Sigma-Models"} Higher Chern-Weil Derivation of AKSZ Sigma-Models
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            on Courant algebroids and relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"}> Branislav Jurco
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Vysoky"} Jan Vysoky
              = succeed "," do
                %em Courant Algebroid Connections and String Effective Actions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.01540"} arXiv:1612.01540
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Xu Xiaomeng,
              %em Twisted Courant algebroids and coisotropic Cartan geometries
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2282"}> arXiv:1206.2282
              )
        .revisedby
